pponent, N'Kiyla Jasmine Thomas, won her primary runoff as a self-described democratic socialist but reported only $456 in cash on hand.\n\nEvery major expert rating, from Cook to the Economist, places the race in Solid or Safe Republican territory, and prediction markets give Democrats just a 2% chance. An August poll showed the Republican leading by roughly 24 points. A public dispute between Hern and interim Senator Armstrong over the swearing-in transition has drawn headlines but is unlikely to alter the race's basic trajectory in such a heavily Republican state.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0081, "margin": -15.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0064, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0068, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.002, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0111, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0041, "margin": -20.0}]}